  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">KOMPASS - Transfer of Skills and Knowledge to Support the Austrian Asylum and Migration Administration with a Focus on Vulnerable Persons</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the project is to contribute to an optimization of processes in the context of asylum and migration in Austria, focusing on vulnerable persons. This will be achieved through capacity building in the following areas: 1. General and specific knowledge of migration; 2. Intercultural competences and communication skills; as well as 3. Human trafficking and other forms of violence, exploitation and abuse, particularly of unaccompanied migrant children (UMC). The acquired competences and knowledge will be applied in the following areas:- In the processing of applications for international protection, settlement or residence, in the context of alien&apos;s procedures and in general official work on asylum and migration. The project activities will benefit actors in the Austrian asylum and migration system, including decision-makers, the Federal Ministry of the Interior (MoI), legal counsellors, care workers, return counsellors, the police, the border patrol, local authorities, child welfare authorities, and organizations that provide support to asylum seekers and migrants.</narrative>
  </description>
